  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added a reproducible, separately hashed PARI 2.17.4 benchmark derivative whose monotonic stage latch exclusively attributes the complete prepared bnfinit0 kernel to relation/retry, sparse HNF/SNF, unit/regulator, honesty/generators/final, and residual stages. Every sample preserves the gap-free ordered segment sequence as well as aggregate totals; the checker reconstructs every total and visit count from those segments. A same-source driver linked to the pristine library supplies the total perturbation control. The focused checker verifies pristine source immutability, exact result/work/all-66-RNG-word equivalence, exact stage conservation, monotonicity, repeated transitions, stable manifest paths, and independently hashed derivative/control artifacts.",
    "risks": [
      "The committed shared-host diagnostic is explicitly unqualified; the enforced 11-pair, one-second-per-mode, <=2% perturbation gate still requires the campaign timing coordinator's quiet pinned Linux host.",
      "Stage names describe source-boundary attribution and are diagnostic labels, not an assertion that every instruction in an interval has a single mathematical purpose.",
      "This benchmark derivative is Linux x86-64 only and must never replace or modify the pristine mathematical authority."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Run the strict perturbation gate on the designated quiet host while preserving the frozen manifest and raw receipt.",
      "Use the exclusive stage record in the end-to-end comparison runner without promoting local timing evidence to an authority claim."
    ]
